    "lawCode": "Amd §1113, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2114\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the insurance law, in relation to\naccelerated life insurance payments for certain chronic conditions\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo provide refined chronic illness triggers for an accelerated death\nbenefit by conforming New York law to the Internal Revenue Code.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend section 1113(a)(1)(C) and (D) of the\ninsurance law to refine the long term care triggers for qualification\nfor an accelerated death benefit under a life insurance policy\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis proposal would amend §1113(a)(1)(C) and (D) of the insurance law\nto refine the long term care triggers for qualification for an\naccelerated death benefit under a life insurance policy. The current\nstandard for triggering payment of an accelerated death benefit for\nchronic illness (i.e., in need of long term care services) is more\nrestrictive than the Internal Revenue Code (IRC § 101(g)), as well as\nother state laws, which require the insured to be certified as having\na chronic illness, but do not require permanent confinement, as\ncurrent New York law does. This proposal removes the requirement for\npermanent confinement and adds a requirement that the insured must be\nchronically ill for a period of at least 90 days, as defined by IRC §\n7702(B).\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
